{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache` is a concrete, cloneable type.\nCloning it shares its state and takes constant time in the number of interned nodes and cached outlines.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct ValidationCache<D: Domain> { /* private fields */ }\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> Clone for ValidationCache<D>;\nimpl<D: Domain> Default for ValidationCache<D>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The two `{test}` items adequately check `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.ValidationCache`. One obligation has no direct test, and I judged it exempt.\n\n**Obligations drawn from the text**\n1. `ValidationCache` is a concrete, cloneable type.\n2. Cloning shares state.\n3. Cloning takes constant time in the number of interned nodes and cached outlines.\n4. `Default` is implemented.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Cloneable and sharing (nodes):** `clones_interning_the_same_data_concurrently_get_one_handle` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` clones the cache into 4 threads. Each thread interns `Node(42)`.\n  - It asserts that all returned ids are equal.\n  - It asserts that the original cache resolves the id with `node_data` to `Node(42)`.\n  - It asserts that a different value (`Node(43)`) gets a different id.\n  - A clone with its own private node table would fail these assertions.\n- **Sharing (outlines):** `domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path` in the same file wraps the cache in `Application` and clones it with `domain.clone()`, which uses the derived `Clone` and so calls `ValidationCache::clone`.\n  - A file loaded through `peer.cache()` is later returned by `domain.cache()` after the file is deleted.\n  - The first successful outline for `path` is reused (`std::ptr::eq` on the outlines), even though the file changed on disk.\n  - A separate `Application::default().cache()` sees the new file contents, so independent caches stay independent.\n  - It also checks that retained snapshots survive after the domains are dropped.\n- **`Default`:** `ValidationCache::new()` is `Self::default()`, as read in `domain.rs#impl[ValidationCache<D>]/fn[new]`. Both tests build their cache with `new()`. The `Application` derive of `Default` also builds fresh caches through `Default`, and the test asserts that a fresh cache has no interned nodes and no cached outline for `path`.\n- **Concrete type:** this is established by the tests naming `ValidationCache::<Application>` directly.\n\n**Not directly tested**\n- **Constant-time cloning:** no test measures it. `impl[ValidationCache<D>/Clone]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` only calls `.clone()` on `Arc` fields and `Option<Arc>` fields, with no conditional and no transformation. This is a pass-through, so I treated it as exempt, and a timing test would be unreliable anyway.\n- **Sharing of `source_addresses`, `sources` and `agent`:** these use the same field-wise `Arc` clone. I did not find a test that exercises sharing for them specifically. I judged this residual risk acceptable, because the two most behavior-bearing shared tables (nodes and outlines) are tested.\n\n**Marking:** both tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement. I found no relevant unmarked test.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
